Subject: [PATCH 5/9] SCH-103: Record passing Linux queue admission gates

Verify make check, make build and go test -p 1 ./internal/modules/... on Linux amd64 at 9709ee193ca70c0e252aa7284b762e80193bd001. All nine real PostgreSQL queued-admission race regressions passed in a disconnected loopback-only namespace on PostgreSQL 18.6 with pgvector 0.8.7.

The qualified rows are persistent owner fixtures, not the installed training dispatcher. Production catalog, fair candidate selection, authenticated consumers and positive physical stop acceptance remain owner integrations. Keep SCH-103 open. The private fixture container, generated audit binary and credential files were removed, and both heavy-test locks were released.
